# Normalise line endings in the repository, not in anyone's editor.
#
# The workflow file went nine commits as CRLF without anyone noticing,
# because GitHub's YAML parser tolerates it. It cost three exchanges
# between two people each holding half the truth: one of us measured the
# blob correctly and the other measured a PowerShell-re-encoded copy.
# A file attribute cannot be forgotten, mis-measured, or re-encoded by a
# shell redirect, so this is the structural fix rather than a discipline.
#
# Everything text in this repo is LF, on checkout as well as in the blob.

* text=auto eol=lf

# Workflow definitions: a trailing CR inside a `run: |` block can change
# shell behaviour (case patterns, literal string comparisons) and is
# invisible in review.
*.yml  text eol=lf
*.yaml text eol=lf

# Shell fragments and Markdown.
*.sh   text eol=lf
*.bash text eol=lf
*.md   text eol=lf

# The xnu patch series must never be silently re-encoded: a stray CR turns
# a hunk into a failed hunk, and the associated context is expensive to
# recover. `diff` and `-p1` both care about these bytes literally.
*.patch text eol=lf
*.diff  text eol=lf

# Source we edit in the workflow but do not own.
*.c    text eol=lf
*.h    text eol=lf
*.py   text eol=lf

# Binary artifacts must be untouched.
*.png  binary
*.jpg  binary
*.jpeg binary
*.gif  binary
*.ico  binary
*.gz   binary
*.bz2  binary
*.xz   binary
*.zst  binary
*.zip  binary
*.img  binary
*.dtb  binary
*.ko   binary
